      "id": 3799,
      "sender_id": 118,
      "content": "<p>hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"25\">@YZ</span> The Playground is very helpful—thank you! I have two feature suggestions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Could <strong>Custom Problem</strong> support importing a CSV or TXT file containing up to 10 problems at a time? Currently, each problem requires pasting the LHS and RHS separately, so testing 10 problems means copying and pasting 20 times. Even better, could users create and save a custom problem set, similar to the built-in <code>normal</code> problem set, and select up to 10 problems from it for each run?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>It seems that other members of the same team cannot view the solvers I uploaded or my run history. Could you also consider supporting team-level sharing or visibility for uploaded solvers and run results? This would make collaboration within a team much easier.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Would either of these be possible?</p>",
