    {
      "id": 3852,
      "sender_id": 534,
      "content": "<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"25\">@YZ</span> , I ran into what looks like a Playground environment or file-permission issue in these three runs:</p>\n<p>s2run_81f3e90d-9d39-457a-87b2-5e977496517a<br>\ns2run_5f065026-b699-441d-a3a6-a7bf48d1160e<br>\ns2run_9521f785-e6a5-465d-8207-73127776a64f</p>\n<p>All three reported the following error:</p>\n<p>Submission.lean:1:0: error: failed to open file 'deps/stage2-judge/.lake/packages/mathlib/.lake/build/lib/lean/Mathlib/Tactic.olean': Permission denied</p>\n<p>It looks like the Mathlib .olean file exists in the evaluation environment, but the Lean process does not have permission to read it. The same generated certificates pass with the official judge locally.</p>\n<p>The first run, s2run_81f3e90d-9d39-457a-87b2-5e977496517a, also took an unusually long time. The same problem and solver finish very quickly locally—roughly two seconds for the solver, followed by a successful judge check—so the long runtime on the Playground may be another infrastructure issue, or possibly related to the failed Mathlib access.</p>\n<p>Could you please check the permissions of the Mathlib build/cache files in the Playground environment, as well as the execution logs for the first run? Thanks!</p>",
      "recipient_id": 43,
      "timestamp": 1787278800,
